    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** serving as the clear offensive anchor. With a score of 66.54, **Merrill** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against Dustin May. The optimization here is driven by a strong platoon advantage (+13%) and a favorable lineup position (+8%), outweighing a slight negative park factor. While **Drake Baldwin** earns a spot at 50.51, his utility is primarily buoyed by his leadoff position; he faces a steep challenge against Yamamoto, whose 3.40 xERA mandates a cautious outlook despite the volume boost **Baldwin** receives from the #1 spot in the order.\n\nThe remainder of the outfield, occupied by **Kyle Tucker** (47.59) and **Andy Pages** (43.88), faces a difficult test against Sale. Both players suffer significant efficiency hits due to Sale's elite SP skill, which dampens their base projections by 19%. **Kyle Tucker** is forced to navigate a suboptimal #8 spot in the order, further suppressing his ceiling today. On the bench, **Luis Lara** was the most viable alternative, finishing with a 35.65 score. Ultimately, the optimizer sidelined **Luis Lara** due to the combination of a daunting matchup against Pivetta and the inherent risk of his \"Lineup Pending\" status, which precluded him from receiving the boost that **Drake Baldwin** secured by being confirmed at the top of the order.\n\nManagement remains sidelined for core assets like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, both of whom are unavailable due to team off-days. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL, limiting our depth in categories like stolen bases where we typically rely on speed-first options. The focus today is on navigating the high-tier pitching volatility while protecting our daily cap with high-probability floor plays like **Jackson Merrill**.",
